  {
    "episode_id": 92915,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92915.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "So I went to clerk for a federal judge in Little Rock, Arkansas. He was a wonderful judge, and this won't surprise people. There weren't a lot of other law clerks who wanted to work on the bankruptcy cases. And so literally, I think I got to work on every single bankruptcy opinion, the entire Eighth Circuit Court of Appeals, which stretches from North Dakota down to Arkansas, worked on that year. And then I went off and I took the bar exam, and I practiced law in Portland, Oregon. for a couple years.",
