    "turn_idx": 60,
    "turn_text": "Very close. I lost, I like to say, I lost before I won. So on election night, you typically have three speeches in California. You have I won, I lost, and we don't know, because it often takes a while to count all the mail ballots. And so I gave the I don't know speech that we don't know. But everybody was crying and telling me, good try. I got all these sympathy calls and sympathy emails. You know, we love you anyway. Nice try. You know, you made a difference, even though you're not going to make a difference kind of things. And then slowly but surely, over the next couple days, took about seven days I won. And so I would get these messages back. Never mind.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_07",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
