  {
    "episode_id": 92915,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92915.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 130,
    "turn_text": "Oh, look, wherever you put me, I'm going to fight for the American people. I mean, I was a professor. I became a professor to understand what was wrong with our laws and how we could make it better. When I'm in the house, that's what I'm thinking about. What's wrong? How can we make it better? It's going to be the same thing whether I would be in the administration, whatever I go on to do after this. These are the fundamental questions. The fundamental question that is motivated my life is how do we achieve economic prosperity for all Americans? And I'm going to keep asking that question, whatever job I'm in. And I mean, look, the house is fun. It's scrappy. It's a little bit chaotic.",
